## Findings

### 1) High: `StartLine` handling for Codex can skip the wrong turn boundaries

`compactCodex` applies `StartLine` over `lines`, but `lines` includes both `response_item` and `token_count` events. The tests/comment describe `StartLine` as a `response_item` offset, so token events can shift the slice and cause off-by-N truncation on resume/checkpoint flows.

```84:89:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/codex.go
	if opts.StartLine > 0 {
		if opts.StartLine >= len(lines) {
			return []byte{}, nil
		}
		lines = lines[opts.StartLine:]
	}
```

```209:237:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/codex.go
// parseCodexLines reads all JSONL lines, keeping response_item and
// token_count event_msg entries.
func parseCodexLines(content []byte) ([]codexLine, error) {
	// ...
			if json.Unmarshal(lineBytes, &cl) == nil {
				if cl.Type == "response_item" || isCodexTokenCountLine(cl) {
					lines = append(lines, cl)
				}
			}
```

**Why this matters:** checkpoint rewind/resume can include extra or missing user/assistant turns depending on how many token events were emitted before the slice point.

---

### 2) Medium: assistant text extraction drops additional `output_text` blocks

Codex assistant messages are parsed as an array, but only the first `output_text` block is returned. If Codex emits multiple text blocks in one assistant message, content is silently truncated.

```311:325:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/codex.go
func codexAssistantText(raw json.RawMessage) string {
	var blocks []struct {
		Type string `json:"type"`
		Text string `json:"text"`
	}
	if json.Unmarshal(raw, &blocks) != nil {
		return ""
	}
	for _, b := range blocks {
		if b.Type == "output_text" && b.Text != "" {
			return b.Text
		}
	}
	return ""
}
```

**Why this matters:** loss of assistant output fidelity in compacted transcripts.

---

## Notes

- I reviewed the branch diff from [`main...support-compact-transcript-all-agents`](https://github.com/entireio/cli/compare/main...support-compact-transcript-all-agents).
- I also ran `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact`; current tests pass, but they don’t cover the two edge cases above.
